| HEV lwIP fork | `2a11c14c7a32887af25a034e82ef18b0b12076ac` | BSD-style 3-clause |
| HEV yaml fork | `efa36117a8646d26d12b58e05bac472d7854a70d` | MIT |

The Apple artifact remains checksum-locked by `NativeDependencies/manifest.json`.
The notice set is present and verified; release packaging must continue to ship
the aggregated MIT text and complete lwIP notice and must compare them against
the actual shipped SBOM. Wintun is outside the Apple binary notice set.

A future fork requires all of the following before authorization:

1. Instruments evidence on the target device/OS identifies bridge copies or
   syscall rate as a material bottleneck.
2. A minimal callback-ingress prototype improves the same measured workload.
3. Public framing, fault, fuzz, backpressure, lifecycle, and memory regression
   suites remain green, including negative tests at the production call site.
4. The patch inventory, exact upstream base, notices, conflict test, upstreaming
   disposition, and rebase procedure are reviewed.

## Residual risks and revalidation triggers

- Re-run the complete physical matrix for a new baseline Mac class, a new major
  macOS release, a Swift/Xcode SDK change affecting NetworkExtension or Darwin
  sockets, or any change to bridge I/O, buffer setup, batching, framing, HEV
  lifecycle, native artifact, compiler flags, or selected HEV graph.
- Re-run memory composition when SSH, DNS, relay, cache, or reconnect-overlap
  allocations land. Exceeding the residual 16,498,688-byte 25 MiB allowance at
  the measured 500-session row reopens the session ceiling; it does not justify
  weakening the memory gate.
- Re-run end-to-end MTU evidence before selecting 4096, and reopen the decision
  on any unexplained nominal loss, family-specific red row, `EMSGSIZE`, clamp
  change, or new fragmentation observation.
- Upstream HEV issue 315 remains an unreproduced teardown risk. Any Apple
  reproduction, upstream lifecycle change, or abnormal stop result reopens the
  lifecycle decision.
- Physical iPhone, jetsam, NAT64, sleep/wake, energy, and whole-extension rows
  remain deferred/blocked, never inferred from macOS or loopback.

